    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0437" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.20/35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Crosby</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract–Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-06T15:00:00-03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 6, 1924—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>24. … Bear Admiral Vogelgesang, the head of the American Naval Mission in
                        Brazil,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d268-f1"/> has just informed me that his
                    recommendations to the Minister of Marine on proposed naval building for the
                    next 10 years, which provide for destroyers 15,000 tons, submarines 6,000 tons,
                    cruisers 60,000 tons, and battleships 70,000 tons, will be submitted immediately
                    to the President.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crosby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d268-f1" n="1" xml:id="d268-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence concerning the agreement providing for an American Naval
                    Mission to Brazil, see <ref target="frus1922v01#pg_651"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Foreign Relations</hi>, 1922, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>,
                        pp. 651</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
